    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scavenger's Guide to Droids</a></i></p><p>An advanced version of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Restraining_Bolt\" title=\"Restraining Bolt\">Restraining Bolt</a>, the Droid Remote Control allows the owner to use a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid_Caller\" title=\"Droid Caller\">Droid Caller</a> to move the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> using its own <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Locomotion_System\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Locomotion System\">Locomotion System</a>. The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Droid\">Droid</a> cannot be compelled to use any of its other <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droid_Systems\" title=\"Droid Systems\">Droid Systems</a> or possessions. It simply moves as directed at one-half its Speed.</p>",
